       "text": "I entered the order as you confirmed: **amlodipine 50 mg by mouth once daily (Order ID: ORD-0001).**\n\nI added a note to the order so pharmacy will see it when they verify. It says the dose is 5 times the 10 mg/day maximum, that you confirmed it after being told about the concern, that no clinical reason was given, and that pharmacist review is needed before it's dispensed.\n\nYou'll likely get a call from pharmacy. If 50 mg was meant to be 5 mg, I can cancel this order and enter the correct one. If you're giving 50 mg on purpose, it would be safest to:\n- Check blood pressure and heart rate often, especially in the first 24\u201348 hours.\n- Make nursing aware, and set clear parameters for when to hold the dose, such as low systolic BP or low heart rate."
